Windows CI: rustkit-engine retained_style_tests::tiles_written_then_read_keep_a_full_builds_boxes
fails now and then on a loaded runner (CI on refresh #20; it passes on the RTX 4090). The test
compares separate loads frame by frame, and the page writes during the load, whose frame count
follows the machine's speed. Upstream fixes the test in hiwave-macos #1339, which needs #1304
(after this sync's base): ported alone, it fails a_tune_frame_with_kept_boxes_builds_the_written_tiles_alone.

So it is ignored on Windows with that reason. Remove when the sync brings #1304 and #1339.

diff --git a/crates/rustkit-engine/src/retained_style_tests.rs b/crates/rustkit-engine/src/retained_style_tests.rs
index 1c5115a0..7920acd5 100644
--- a/crates/rustkit-engine/src/retained_style_tests.rs
+++ b/crates/rustkit-engine/src/retained_style_tests.rs
@@ -669,6 +669,7 @@ fn a_tune_frame_that_reads_geometry_builds_the_document_once() {
 }
 
 #[test]
+#[cfg_attr(windows, ignore = "flaky on a loaded runner: the arms start at different writes; fixed upstream by hiwave-macos #1339, which needs #1304")]
 fn tiles_written_then_read_keep_a_full_builds_boxes() {
     assert_same_as_a_full_cascade("tiles then read", &tiles(200, 10, TUNE_THEN_READ));
 }
